& [PortionSliceMapV1] is the slice-ready whole-pie decomposition map for LangSOP
  + [map_state] is ready_for_deeper_reasoning_design_slices
  + [slice_policy] is portions bake the whole product; slice families divide portions; slices are minted just in time from readiness
  + [rebake_trigger] is source change, authority change, portion boundary change, completed-work delta, stale support, false-ready slice, new safety risk, or implementation contradiction

  = must: load this map before minting LangSOP development slices
  = must: update this map after completed work changes support or requirements
  = must: keep blocked portions visible but unsliced except for blocker-resolution or preparation work

& [Portion: P1SemanticAuthorityAndSourceLineage] is supported
  + [portion_id] is P1
  + [portion_name] is semantic authority and source lineage
  + [purpose] is preserve SOP source, SJS signatures, source snapshots, canonical authority, and soft-wire reconsideration
  + [dependency_set] is none for planning use
  + [support_record] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Initial_Workflow.v2.canonical.sop
  + [support_record] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Whole_Pie_Working_Pattern.canonical.sop
  + [proof_route] is signature validation over source manifests and satisfaction signatures
  + [surface_ref] is manager, narrative, debug, and worker packet authority notices
  + [slice_family] is source-preservation-and-signature-validation

  = must: remain loaded as authority context for every other portion

& [Portion: P2AuthorityKernelAndRecordSchemas] is ready_for_slice_family
  + [portion_id] is P2
  + [portion_name] is authority kernel and record schemas
  + [purpose] is define logical records, natural keys, lineage, authority states, readiness states, and freshness rules
  + [dependency_set] is P1
  + [support_record] is CanonicalKernelRecordContractV2
  + [support_gap] is record-specific schemas not yet drafted
  + [support_gap] is natural-key matrix not yet accepted
  + [support_gap] is physical storage not yet chosen
  + [proof_route] is schema fixtures for valid, stale, blocked, contradicted, and invalid records
  + [slice_family] is kernel-record-schema-design
  + [slice_family] is natural-key-and-state-matrix
  + [slice_family] is storage-decision-after-logical-schema

  = must: start with deeper-reasoning slices

& [Portion: P3CompiledSOPOperatorContracts] is ready_for_slice_family
  + [portion_id] is P3
  + [portion_name] is compiled SOP operator contracts
  + [purpose] is define the common operator contract that lets stable SOP duties become traceable mechanical operators
  + [dependency_set] is P1
  + [dependency_set] is P2 for implementation
  + [support_record] is CanonicalOperatorContractV2
  + [support_gap] is template not yet authored
  + [support_gap] is first operator examples not yet accepted
  + [proof_route] is example contracts for signature_validation and support_readiness_recompute
  + [slice_family] is operator-contract-template-design
  + [slice_family] is signature-validation-operator-contract
  + [slice_family] is support-readiness-operator-contract

  = must: keep template design in deeper-reasoning mode
  = should: make later operator examples GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after template acceptance

& [Portion: P4WholeFieldPlanningAndPacketization] is blocked
  + [portion_id] is P4
  + [portion_name] is whole-field planning and packetization
  + [purpose] is derive readiness projections, packet candidates, blocker-resolution slices, and completion-review gates
  + [dependency_set] is P2
  + [dependency_set] is P3
  + [support_gap] is readiness operator not yet defined
  + [support_gap] is work-packet generator not yet proved
  + [proof_route] is fixture capability field that produces ready, blocked, stale, unsupported, and verified cases
  + [slice_family] is support-readiness-operator
  + [slice_family] is work-packet-generator
  + [slice_family] is completion-review-delta-gate

  = must: not mint implementation slices until readiness and packetization contracts exist
  = may: mint preparation slices to define those contracts

& [Portion: P5LangGraphProcedureRuntime] is blocked
  + [portion_id] is P5
  + [portion_name] is LangGraph procedure runtime
  + [purpose] is execute compiled operators over kernel records with checkpointed procedure state and judgment interrupts
  + [dependency_set] is P2
  + [dependency_set] is P3
  + [dependency_set] is P8 fixture pack
  + [support_gap] is graph proof-of-shape not implemented
  + [proof_route] is graph run over fixture records with expected operator traces
  + [slice_family] is whole-field-planner-graph-proof
  + [slice_family] is graph-interrupt-fixtures

  = must: keep LangGraph checkpoint state non-authoritative
  = should: route graph proof implementation to GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark after contracts and fixtures stabilize

& [Portion: P6SurfaceProjectionSystem] is blocked
  + [portion_id] is P6
  + [portion_name] is surface projection system
  + [purpose] is render manager, worker, narrative, debug, chat, Codex, terminal, IRC, Matrix, web, and optional Langflow projections from kernel records
  + [dependency_set] is P2
  + [dependency_set] is P4
  + [dependency_set] is P8 fixture pack
  + [support_gap] is projection fixtures not yet generated
  + [proof_route] is projection snapshots with authority_notice, freshness_rule, and blocked/stale visibility
  + [slice_family] is manager-worker-debug-surface-projections
  + [slice_family] is chat-and-adapter-projection-contracts
  + [slice_family] is langflow-export-prototype

  = must: never let surfaces mutate canonical authority directly
  = should: route bounded projection rendering to GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark after fixture records exist

